-Robert Ludlum?

788
00:31:55,740 --> 00:31:57,200
-Look, why can't I
 work on this case?

789
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:58,960
-Go back to your desk.

790
00:31:58,960 --> 00:32:00,760
-Yes, sir.

791
00:32:00,760 --> 00:32:01,260
-And Kelton.

792
00:32:01,260 --> 00:32:02,470
-Yes, sir?

793
00:32:02,470 --> 00:32:03,110
-Kiss the birdie.

794
00:32:03,110 --> 00:32:05,240
-I told the boy to bring
 the papers in himself.

795
00:32:05,240 --> 00:32:05,960
-Yes, sir.

796
00:32:05,960 --> 00:32:06,800
But if you ask me--

797
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,600
-I didn't.

798
00:32:08,600 --> 00:32:09,580
-Yes, sir.

799
00:32:09,580 --> 00:32:10,290
-And Kelton?

800
00:32:10,290 --> 00:32:11,590
-Yes, sir.

801
00:32:11,590 --> 00:32:13,090
Where's Lieutenant Craig?

802
00:32:13,090 --> 00:32:14,410
-In his office, I think.

803
00:32:14,410 --> 00:32:15,300
-Send him in.

804
00:32:15,300 --> 00:32:15,960
-Yes, sir.

805
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:16,970
Right away, sir.

806
00:32:16,970 --> 00:32:18,070
-And get me my index finger.

807
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:21,610
-Wait a minute.

808
00:32:21,610 --> 00:32:24,630
There's bird poopy on my paper.

809
00:32:24,630 --> 00:32:26,130
-Oh, let me see here.

810
00:32:26,130 --> 00:32:28,540
Ed Wood caught wearing a dress?

811
00:32:28,540 --> 00:32:30,820
Again?

812
00:32:30,820 --> 00:32:34,370
-I just don't get
 that Gary Larson.

813
00:32:34,370 --> 00:32:35,650
-Oh, I'm beat.

814
00:32:39,170 --> 00:32:44,870
-Doo doo doot doo doo doo doo

815
00:32:44,870 --> 00:32:47,600
-No one will be seated during
 the gripping water cooler

816
00:32:47,600 --> 00:32:48,510
scene.

817
00:32:48,510 --> 00:32:50,790
-You know, installing
 this Rumplemintz

818
00:32:50,790 --> 00:32:52,340
cooler was great idea.

819
00:32:57,230 --> 00:32:58,840
ALL: Finish it.

820
00:32:58,840 --> 00:32:59,660
Finish it!

821
00:32:59,660 --> 00:33:01,760
-Come on!

822
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:02,930
-Hi, Bavara.

823
00:33:02,930 --> 00:33:03,660
-Hello, Dick.

824
00:33:03,660 --> 00:33:04,490
Sit down.

825
00:33:04,490 --> 00:33:06,590
-Now, say hello to the bird.

826
00:33:06,590 --> 00:33:08,470
-Is there anyone who hasn't?

827
00:33:08,470 --> 00:33:09,600
-You can say that again.

828
00:33:09,600 --> 00:33:11,340
-There's one nice
 thing about birds.

829
00:33:11,340 --> 00:33:13,180
They never cause
 anybody any trouble.

830
00:33:13,180 --> 00:33:14,490
-Yeah, tell that
 to Tippy Hedren.

831
00:33:14,490 --> 00:33:16,250
-Your girlfriend
 writes a good story.

832
00:33:16,250 --> 00:33:17,400
-She thinks so.

833
00:33:17,400 --> 00:33:18,420
Anything new?

834
00:33:18,420 --> 00:33:18,920
-No.

835
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:19,680
-You?

836
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:23,240
-12 disappearances around this
 place and nothing to go on.

837
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:25,060
-And nothing this time, either.

838
00:33:25,060 --> 00:33:27,420
-I've been around that
 swamp so many times

839
00:33:27,420 --> 00:33:29,130
I'm getting web footed.

840
00:33:29,130 --> 00:33:31,080
-Well, don't kill me over it.

841
00:33:31,080 --> 00:33:32,720
-It's been fired recently.

842
00:33:32,720 --> 00:33:34,570
-It's been fired
 several times recently.

843
00:33:34,570 --> 00:33:36,110
-Taking target
 practice on the bird.

844
00:33:36,110 --> 00:33:38,550
-Identified it a
 little while ago.

845
00:33:38,550 --> 00:33:41,120
The coat belonged to
 Leif McCray, his partner.

846
00:33:41,120 --> 00:33:41,990
-You want it?

847
00:33:41,990 --> 00:33:44,000
-Went hunting out by Marsh Lake.

848
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:45,290
Never returned.

849
00:33:45,290 --> 00:33:46,350
-Not much left of it.

850
00:33:46,350 --> 00:33:48,210
-The boys found it
 floating in the lake.

851
00:33:48,210 --> 00:33:49,580
-What about the rifle?

852
00:33:49,580 --> 00:33:51,540
-About a mile from
 the old Willow place.

853
00:33:51,540 --> 00:33:52,540
-All ties together.

854
00:33:52,540 --> 00:33:54,230
-But it doesn't prove anything.

855
00:33:54,230 --> 00:33:57,060
-You think there's anything
 in these monster stories?

856
00:33:57,060 --> 00:33:58,130
-Your girlfriend does.

857
00:33:58,130 --> 00:33:59,530
-Leave her out of this.

858
00:33:59,530 --> 00:34:01,490
-The police don't
 believe in monsters.

859
00:34:01,490 --> 00:34:02,820
Facts are our business.

860
00:34:02,820 --> 00:34:04,070
Facts and only facts.

861
00:34:04,070 --> 00:34:05,530
And don't you forget it.

862
00:34:05,530 --> 00:34:07,570
-I'm telling you the
 captain doesn't see nobody.

863
00:34:07,570 --> 00:34:09,110
-He'll want to see these.

864
00:34:09,110 --> 00:34:13,830
-Captain Robbins, will you tell
 this junior G-man to let me go?

865
00:34:13,830 --> 00:34:14,360
-Kelton.

866
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:14,860
-Yes, sir?

867
00:34:14,860 --> 00:34:16,250
-Let her go.

868
00:34:16,250 --> 00:34:19,510
It's Ed Wood's cameo
 appearance here.

869
00:34:19,510 --> 00:34:21,270
-It used to be a
 newspaper reporter

870
00:34:21,270 --> 00:34:23,400
could get information
 around this place.

871
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:24,320
-For a small fee.

872
00:34:24,320 --> 00:34:25,770
-What in the world do you mean?

873
00:34:25,770 --> 00:34:28,050
-Now he makes like a comic.

874
00:34:28,050 --> 00:34:28,710
Dick Craig.

875
00:34:28,710 --> 00:34:30,690
I don't put much stock
 in the future success

876
00:34:30,690 --> 00:34:32,320
of our married life
 if already you're

877
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:33,580
holding out secrets on me.

878
00:34:33,580 --> 00:34:34,080
-Hmm?

879
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:36,180
-You've been dodging me all day.

880
00:34:36,180 --> 00:34:36,680
-Have we met?

881
00:34:36,680 --> 00:34:37,840
-Where'd you get
 an idea like that?

882
00:34:37,840 --> 00:34:39,510
-You mean you haven't
 been dodging me?

883
00:34:39,510 --> 00:34:40,770
-I was actively avoiding you.

884
00:34:40,770 --> 00:34:43,030
-And all those times
 I called and Kelton

885
00:34:43,030 --> 00:34:45,300
said the line was
 busy, it really was.

886
00:34:45,300 --> 00:34:46,260
-Yes.

887
00:34:46,260 --> 00:34:46,760
-OK.

888
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:49,690
Let's have the story on
 Lake Marsh and the monster.

889
00:34:49,690 --> 00:34:51,950
-Ah, monster, monster.

890
00:34:51,950 --> 00:34:53,000
-Who's got the monster?

891
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,760
-I thought so.

892
00:34:54,760 --> 00:34:55,990
-There are no such
 thing as monsters.

893
00:34:55,990 --> 00:34:57,660
This is the 20th century.

894
00:34:57,660 --> 00:34:59,240
-Don't count on it.

895
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:00,440
Monsters, I mean.

896
00:35:00,440 --> 00:35:01,130
-Now, Janet.

897
00:35:01,130 --> 00:35:01,970
-Dammit.

898
00:35:01,970 --> 00:35:03,090
-Don't you "Now, Janet" me.

899
00:35:03,090 --> 00:35:04,940
And you can count
 our engagement off.

900
00:35:04,940 --> 00:35:05,890
-You don't mean that.

901
00:35:05,890 --> 00:35:06,820
-Yes, I do.

902
00:35:06,820 --> 00:35:08,120
-No, she doesn't.

903
00:35:08,120 --> 00:35:09,930
-I most certainly do.

904
00:35:09,930 --> 00:35:11,430
-Well, then give
 him back the ring.

905
00:35:11,430 --> 00:35:12,110
-What?

906
00:35:12,110 --> 00:35:13,120
-This is the best bit.

907
00:35:13,120 --> 00:35:14,540
-Give him back the ring.

908
00:35:14,540 --> 00:35:15,240
-Now, Chief!

909
00:35:15,240 --> 00:35:15,740
I--

910
00:35:15,740 --> 00:35:16,530
-Captain.

911
00:35:16,530 --> 00:35:18,020
Give him back the rock.

912
00:35:18,020 --> 00:35:19,890
It's the only fair thing.

913
00:35:19,890 --> 00:35:23,600
-I'd rather throw it
 in Lake Marsh, first.

914
00:35:23,600 --> 00:35:25,720
Besides, we've got to leave
 our personal lives out

915
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:26,510
of our business lives.

916
00:35:26,510 --> 00:35:27,360
-As it should be.

917
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:29,390
-As I've been saying all along.

918
00:35:29,390 --> 00:35:29,980
-Dog.

919
00:35:29,980 --> 00:35:30,480
[APPLAUSE]

920
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:32,460
-Aw, they used to do
 this in Vaudeville.

921
00:35:32,460 --> 00:35:33,230
-That's your own story.

922
00:35:33,230 --> 00:35:35,290
You wrote it, and
 you're stuck with it.

923
00:35:35,290 --> 00:35:37,230
There's no such as monsters.

924
00:35:37,230 --> 00:35:40,760
[INSANE LAUGHTER]

925
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:41,930
-That makes twelve
 in three months.

926
00:35:41,930 --> 00:35:49,240
[THEME MUSIC]

927
00:35:49,240 --> 00:35:52,800
-Well, looks like I've run
 into it a dead end around here.

928
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:54,940
-I think I'll go
 ruin another movie.

929
00:35:54,940 --> 00:35:57,370
-If you boys want to
 play a game of secrets,

930
00:35:57,370 --> 00:35:59,080
there's nothing left
 for me to do but take

931
00:35:59,080 --> 00:36:01,620
a run out to Lake Marsh, myself.

932
00:36:01,620 --> 00:36:04,060
-Over my dead body.

933
00:36:04,060 --> 00:36:05,740
-That could be arranged.

934
00:36:05,740 --> 00:36:07,750
-It's Lawrencia Bembenek.

935
00:36:07,750 --> 00:36:09,490
-Goodbye.

936
00:36:09,490 --> 00:36:11,030
-Say goodbye to the
 bird, he's hurting.

937
00:36:14,970 --> 00:36:16,570
-Eh, dames.

938
00:36:16,570 --> 00:36:18,540
-She's just crazy enough
 to do what she says.

939
00:36:18,540 --> 00:36:20,280
-You know what, Captain?

940
00:36:20,280 --> 00:36:21,200
-That's what.

941
00:36:21,200 --> 00:36:22,170
-I think you're right.

942
00:36:24,950 --> 00:36:27,260
-Let's see, who
 else can I frighten?

943
00:36:27,260 --> 00:36:30,130
-And we now return
 to "The Big Big Car."

944
00:36:30,130 --> 00:36:32,280
-Geez, you could stand
 up in that thing.

945
00:36:35,740 --> 00:36:40,470
-Oh, the sign says, "Space
 Reserved for Creepy Woman.

946
00:36:44,110 --> 00:36:45,630
-This is Lake Marsh?

947
00:36:45,630 --> 00:36:48,470
-Well, they paved Lake Marsh
 and put up a parking lot.

948
00:36:52,060 --> 00:36:52,950
-Oh, that's the door.

949
00:36:52,950 --> 00:36:53,710
I wouldn't have--

950
00:36:53,710 --> 00:36:56,680
-Self-styling a
 door [INAUDIBLE].

951
00:36:56,680 --> 00:36:57,950
-Hi, Tillie.

952
00:36:57,950 --> 00:36:58,770
-Hi, Janet.

953
00:36:58,770 --> 00:37:00,470
Long time no see.

954
00:37:00,470 --> 00:37:02,090
-Tillie, do you remember
 a couple of years

955
00:37:02,090 --> 00:37:04,860
ago, in the real estate section,
 when the old Willow place out

956
00:37:04,860 --> 00:37:07,690
on Lake Marsh was up for
 sale-- against back taxes?

957
00:37:07,690 --> 00:37:08,190
ALL: Yeah!

958
00:37:08,190 --> 00:37:13,290
-Seems to me, that was around
 November or December of '48.

959
00:37:13,290 --> 00:37:14,260
Want to see the files?

960
00:37:14,260 --> 00:37:14,890
-Yes.

961
00:37:14,890 --> 00:37:16,270
-Just a minute.

962
00:37:16,270 --> 00:37:19,120
-That was right after my face
 went over to the dark side.

963
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:19,830
-Here we are.

964
00:37:19,830 --> 00:37:21,820
-Ah, no, that's
 my brownie recipe.

965
00:37:21,820 --> 00:37:24,160
-October to December '48.

966
00:37:24,160 --> 00:37:25,470
In the file cabinet over there.

967
00:37:25,470 --> 00:37:26,600
-I won't be long.

968
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:27,390
-Take your time.

969
00:37:27,390 --> 00:37:28,330
I ain't going any place.

970
00:37:28,330 --> 00:37:30,240
And neither are they.

971
00:37:30,240 --> 00:37:32,940
-It's Wilhelmina Demarest.

972
00:37:32,940 --> 00:37:35,740
-Huh, what do you know,
 building codes under fire.

973
00:37:35,740 --> 00:37:36,800
-Hey, don't touch that sandwich.

974
00:37:39,430 --> 00:37:41,250
-Oh, there's a
 column in Ann Landers

975
00:37:41,250 --> 00:37:44,100
about older women
 liking cuddling.

976
00:37:44,100 --> 00:37:45,000
-What's she-- ew.

977
00:37:48,210 --> 00:37:49,470
-Find what you wanted, Janet?

978
00:37:49,470 --> 00:37:50,180
-Yes, thanks.

979
00:37:50,180 --> 00:37:52,080
Sorry to leave such
 a mess for you.

980
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:53,600
-Well, that's what
 I get paid for.

981
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:54,660
-Be a dear, Tillie.

982
00:37:54,660 --> 00:37:56,110
Call the boss--

983
00:37:56,110 --> 00:37:56,800
-Springsteen?

984
00:37:56,800 --> 00:37:57,880
-I'll report in later.

985
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:59,250
-Sure thing.

986
00:37:59,250 --> 00:38:00,770
Find something hot?

987
00:38:00,770 --> 00:38:02,260
-Could be.

988
00:38:02,260 --> 00:38:03,280
Oh, and Dick!

989
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:05,110
-Oh, yes.

990
00:38:05,110 --> 00:38:06,850
Break my dinner date with him.

991
00:38:06,850 --> 00:38:09,350
Tell him I-- Oh, I have
 an ulcer or something.

992
00:38:09,350 --> 00:38:10,900
-Leave it to me.

993
00:38:10,900 --> 00:38:12,190
I fix.

994
00:38:12,190 --> 00:38:14,270
-What's it like outside?

995
00:38:14,270 --> 00:38:15,440
-Hi, Janet.

996
00:38:15,440 --> 00:38:16,040
-Oh, hi, Marge.

997
00:38:16,040 --> 00:38:16,540
-Janet.

998
00:38:16,540 --> 00:38:18,020
Still on the monster hunt?

999
00:38:18,020 --> 00:38:19,020
-What do you think?

1000
00:38:19,020 --> 00:38:21,730
-I think the boss has been
 looking for you all day.

1001
00:38:21,730 --> 00:38:24,410
Something about the police
 wanting those monster stories

1002
00:38:24,410 --> 00:38:25,510
86'ed.

1003
00:38:25,510 --> 00:38:27,380
You've got the whole
 town in a panic.

1004
00:38:27,380 --> 00:38:28,940
-I didn't hear you.

1005
00:38:28,940 --> 00:38:29,800
-I said--

1006
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:30,660
-I know what you said.

1007
00:38:30,660 --> 00:38:31,830
But I didn't hear you.

1008
00:38:31,830 --> 00:38:33,050
-Big face theater.

1009
00:38:33,050 --> 00:38:33,920
-I get it.

1010
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:34,830
See you later.

1011
00:38:34,830 --> 00:38:36,610
-Dun de da da da-- Ahh!

1012
00:38:44,510 --> 00:38:46,480
-Hey, scootch over, Mr. Hoffa.

1013
00:38:52,510 --> 00:38:53,340
-Now, now, Mrs. Webb, no.

1014
00:38:53,340 --> 00:38:53,840
No.

1015
00:38:53,840 --> 00:38:54,460
Slowly, Mrs. Webb.

1016
00:38:54,460 --> 00:38:55,510
Uh, you are backing up.

1017
00:38:55,510 --> 00:38:58,670
You're ba-- Mrs. Webb--

1018
00:38:58,670 --> 00:39:01,540
-[INAUDIBLE] is very
 important in this case.

1019
00:39:01,540 --> 00:39:03,850
-I'd like him to hear
 what you just told me.

1020
00:39:03,850 --> 00:39:05,310
-I should be happy to cooperate.

1021
00:39:05,310 --> 00:39:06,100
-Oh, hello, Dick.

1022
00:39:06,100 --> 00:39:07,830
-Ah, kiss the bird, Dick.

1023
00:39:07,830 --> 00:39:10,260
-Professor Vladimir Strowski,

1024
00:39:10,260 --> 00:39:10,820
-Yeah, right.

1025
00:39:10,820 --> 00:39:12,400
-Glad to meet you, Professor.

1026
00:39:12,400 --> 00:39:13,420
-How do you do?

1027
00:39:13,420 --> 00:39:15,670
-Professor, will you
 bring him up to date?

1028
00:39:15,670 --> 00:39:17,300
-(German accent) Well, I
 was born in Krankenheim.

1029
00:39:17,300 --> 00:39:18,490
My father--

1030
00:39:18,490 --> 00:39:20,600
-Have you ever
 heard of Loch Ness?

1031
00:39:20,600 --> 00:39:22,190
-Any relation to Elliott Ness?

1032
00:39:22,190 --> 00:39:24,000
-It's a lake in
 Scotland, isn't it?

1033
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:25,580
-No, it's a lake in Scotland.

1034
00:39:25,580 --> 00:39:29,880
-Then perhaps you are familiar
 with the Loch Ness Monster.

1035
00:39:29,880 --> 00:39:32,540
-That's a monster in a
 lake in Scotland, right?

1036
00:39:32,540 --> 00:39:35,280
-A few years ago, was called
 in by the British police

1037
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:39,360
to investigate the appearance
 of a monster in Loch Ness.

1038
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:42,120
We thought that it was
 some creature left over

1039
00:39:42,120 --> 00:39:44,710
from a bygone age.

1040
00:39:44,710 --> 00:39:47,600
I am considered an
 authority on the subject

1041
00:39:47,600 --> 00:39:49,890
of prehistoric monsters.

1042
00:39:49,890 --> 00:39:52,350
-He's smelling his thumb.

1043
00:39:52,350 --> 00:39:55,310
-However, I must admit that
 my investigation failed

1044
00:39:55,310 --> 00:39:58,020
to get the desired
 results in that I

1045
00:39:58,020 --> 00:39:59,960
did not see the monster myself.

1046
00:39:59,960 --> 00:40:02,310
-Hey, Siegfried, pick an accent
 and stick with it, will ya?

1047
00:40:02,310 --> 00:40:04,390
-There are sworn statements.

1048
00:40:04,390 --> 00:40:04,970
-Professor--

1049
00:40:04,970 --> 00:40:05,870
-Lunch, yeah.

1050
00:40:05,870 --> 00:40:08,720
-Is it your theory that
 perhaps the Loch Ness Monster

1051
00:40:08,720 --> 00:40:11,510
crossed the ocean and
 came to the swamp?

1052
00:40:11,510 --> 00:40:14,440
-I consider that possibility
 extremely remote.

1053
